{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791562675,"nonce":"8m9E/4/48H9soHKSTabOqdkNZHo=","title":"Tiered: an error left pending after a rebuild is not found by take_pending_error","message":"After `TieredRuntime::finalize_runtime_symbols()` (which rebuilds the JIT module and restores every loaded module), a call that stores into the error-flag global leaves nothing `take_pending_error` can see. Reproduces at d6c594565db161b4c37c63393a5b7b9d19a4a09a with one module and no joins, whether or not the function ran before the rebuild. In crates/zyntax_embed/tests/pending_error.rs terms:\n\n    let mut runtime = TieredRuntime::development().expect(\"runtime\");\n    runtime.set_error_flag_global(\"failure\");\n    runtime.compile_typed_program(program()).expect(\"program compiles\");\n    runtime.finalize_runtime_symbols().expect(\"rebuild\");\n    runtime.call_raw(\"fail\", \u0026[ZyntaxValue::Int(3)]).expect(\"fail runs\");\n    assert_eq!(runtime.take_pending_error(), Some(3)); // left: None\n\nThe same holds after joined pieces (`join_typed_program`) and for the first program's `fail` once pieces joined. `refresh_error_flags` runs after the rebuild and re-reads the slots from the backend, so the slot list and the storage `fail` writes disagree after the rebuild. Not yet established which side is stale: the interpreter's global bindings made at compile time, or code still installed in the cells from before the rebuild (the backend's `rebuild_with_accumulated_symbols` documents that tier-0 code issued before it keeps its old pointers).","files":null}]}